{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Evaluación y comparación de modelos\n",
        "\n",
        "En las secciones anteriores construimos modelos de Gradient Boosting y aprendimos a utilizar Cross-Validation para seleccionar hiperparámetros.\n",
        "\n",
        "Ahora integraremos estos elementos dentro de un flujo completo de aprendizaje automático.\n",
        "\n",
        "Al finalizar esta práctica seremos capaces de:\n",
        "\n",
        "- establecer una **baseline**;\n",
        "- comparar diferentes modelos utilizando los mismos folds;\n",
        "- analizar el desempeño promedio y su variabilidad;\n",
        "- realizar una optimización de hiperparámetros;\n",
        "- recuperar y reajustar el modelo seleccionado;\n",
        "- evaluar finalmente el procedimiento sobre el conjunto de prueba;\n",
        "- analizar predicciones y residuos.\n",
        "\n",
        "Nuestro flujo de trabajo será:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\\boxed{\\text{Datos}}\n",
        "\\longrightarrow\n",
        "\\boxed{\\text{Train/Test}}\n",
        "\\longrightarrow\n",
        "\\boxed{\\text{Cross-Validation}}\n",
        "\\longrightarrow\n",
        "\\boxed{\\text{Comparación}}\n",
        "\\longrightarrow\n",
        "\\boxed{\\text{Tuning}}\n",
        "\\longrightarrow\n",
        "\\boxed{\\text{Refit}}\n",
        "\\longrightarrow\n",
        "\\boxed{\\text{Evaluación final}}.$$\n",
        "\n",
        "::::: diapositivas\n",
        "::: diapositivas-title\n",
        "📝 **Diapositivas**\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::: diapositivas-body\n",
        "[Ver diapositivas](https://github.com/CursosENESJuriquilla/TS_Aprendizaje_de_Maquina_2027-1/blob/main/Material/3.6_ComparacionDeModelos.pdf)\n",
        ":::\n",
        ":::::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Preparación\n",
        "\n",
        "Importamos las bibliotecas necesarias."
      ],
      "id": "109e64e5"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "\n",
        "from time import perf_counter\n",
        "\n",
        "from sklearn.datasets import fetch_california_housing\n",
        "\n",
        "from sklearn.model_selection import (\n",
        "    train_test_split,\n",
        "    KFold,\n",
        "    cross_validate,\n",
        "    RandomizedSearchCV\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "from sklearn.dummy import DummyRegressor\n",
        "from sklearn.linear_model import LinearRegression\n",
        "from sklearn.tree import DecisionTreeRegressor\n",
        "from sklearn.ensemble import (\n",
        "    RandomForestRegressor,\n",
        "    GradientBoostingRegressor\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "from sklearn.metrics import (\n",
        "    mean_absolute_error,\n",
        "    mean_squared_error,\n",
        "    r2_score\n",
        ")"
      ],
      "id": "86758b71",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Cargamos nuevamente California Housing."
      ],
      "id": "f78f0ca2"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "housing = fetch_california_housing(as_frame=True)\n",
        "\n",
        "X = housing.data\n",
        "y = housing.target"
      ],
      "id": "9506c984",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Realizamos la misma partición que utilizamos en las prácticas anteriores."
      ],
      "id": "9a83edf8"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "X_train, X_test, y_train, y_test = train_test_split(\n",
        "    X,\n",
        "    y,\n",
        "    test_size=0.20,\n",
        "    random_state=42\n",
        ")"
      ],
      "id": "bb51460d",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "print(\"Train:\", X_train.shape)\n",
        "print(\"Test: \", X_test.shape)"
      ],
      "id": "2e53c0c4",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "::: callout-important\n",
        "## Última práctica: el test sigue cerrado\n",
        "\n",
        "Todavía no utilizaremos `X_test` ni `y_test`.\n",
        "\n",
        "Primero realizaremos toda la comparación y selección utilizando exclusivamente los datos de entrenamiento.\n",
        "\n",
        "Abriremos el test solamente al final.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## ¿Contra qué debemos comparar?\n",
        "\n",
        "Antes de construir modelos complejos necesitamos una referencia sencilla.\n",
        "\n",
        "Para ello utilizaremos `DummyRegressor`."
      ],
      "id": "a3c44e19"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "baseline = DummyRegressor(\n",
        "    strategy=\"mean\"\n",
        ")"
      ],
      "id": "836747d7",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Este modelo predice esencialmente una cantidad constante basada en la respuesta observada durante el entrenamiento.\n",
        "\n",
        "Por sí mismo no pretende ser un buen modelo.\n",
        "\n",
        "Su función es responder una pregunta mucho más importante:\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.callout-warning icon=\"false\"}\n",
        "## 🧠 Pregunta\n",
        "\n",
        "¿Nuestros modelos realmente están aprendiendo estructura útil en los datos?\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Modelos que compararemos\n",
        "\n",
        "Consideraremos cinco modelos:"
      ],
      "id": "3bc6073b"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "modelos = {\n",
        "    \"Baseline\": DummyRegressor(\n",
        "        strategy=\"mean\"\n",
        "    ),\n",
        "\n",
        "    \"Linear Regression\": LinearRegression(),\n",
        "\n",
        "    \"Decision Tree\": DecisionTreeRegressor(\n",
        "        random_state=42\n",
        "    ),\n",
        "\n",
        "    \"Random Forest\": RandomForestRegressor(\n",
        "        n_estimators=200,\n",
        "        random_state=42,\n",
        "        n_jobs=1\n",
        "    ),\n",
        "\n",
        "    \"Gradient Boosting\": GradientBoostingRegressor(\n",
        "        n_estimators=200,\n",
        "        learning_rate=0.05,\n",
        "        max_depth=2,\n",
        "        random_state=42\n",
        "    )\n",
        "}"
      ],
      "id": "81c344b2",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Observen que estamos comparando modelos con características muy diferentes.\n",
        "\n",
        "Tenemos desde una baseline extremadamente sencilla hasta métodos de ensamble.\n",
        "\n",
        "::: callout-note\n",
        "## Primera comparación\n",
        "\n",
        "En esta primera etapa no intentaremos optimizar exhaustivamente todos los modelos.\n",
        "\n",
        "Queremos obtener una comparación inicial utilizando un procedimiento común de evaluación.\n",
        "\n",
        "Posteriormente realizaremos tuning sobre algunos de los modelos.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Una estrategia común de Cross-Validation\n",
        "\n",
        "Utilizaremos exactamente los mismos folds para todos los modelos."
      ],
      "id": "35d7458c"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "cv = KFold(\n",
        "    n_splits=5,\n",
        "    shuffle=True,\n",
        "    random_state=42\n",
        ")"
      ],
      "id": "c8ceebcc",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Esto significa que cada modelo será entrenado y evaluado sobre las mismas particiones.\n",
        "\n",
        "Conceptualmente queremos:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\\boxed{\n",
        "\\text{mismos datos}\n",
        "+\n",
        "\\text{mismos folds}\n",
        "+\n",
        "\\text{mismas métricas}\n",
        "}.$$\n",
        "\n",
        "## Evaluaremos más de una métrica\n",
        "\n",
        "Hasta ahora utilizamos principalmente RMSE.\n",
        "\n",
        "En esta práctica utilizaremos:\n",
        "\n",
        "- MAE;\n",
        "- RMSE;\n",
        "- $R^2$.\n",
        "\n",
        "Definimos las métricas:"
      ],
      "id": "1af63884"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "scoring = {\n",
        "    \"MAE\": \"neg_mean_absolute_error\",\n",
        "    \"RMSE\": \"neg_root_mean_squared_error\",\n",
        "    \"R2\": \"r2\"\n",
        "}"
      ],
      "id": "3ec7b8a0",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Recordemos que `scikit-learn` devuelve MAE y RMSE negativos cuando se utilizan como *scores*.\n",
        "\n",
        "Esto permite mantener la convención\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\\text{score mayor}\n",
        "\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad\n",
        "\\text{mejor}.$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Después cambiaremos el signo para recuperar los errores en su interpretación habitual.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Comparación mediante Cross-Validation\n",
        "\n",
        "Utilizaremos `cross_validate()`.\n",
        "\n",
        "A diferencia de `cross_val_score()`, esta función nos permite calcular varias métricas simultáneamente y registrar tiempos de entrenamiento."
      ],
      "id": "975f4ff4"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "resultados = []\n",
        "\n",
        "for nombre, modelo in modelos.items():\n",
        "\n",
        "    cv_result = cross_validate(\n",
        "        modelo,\n",
        "        X_train,\n",
        "        y_train,\n",
        "        cv=cv,\n",
        "        scoring=scoring,\n",
        "        n_jobs=1\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "    resultados.append({\n",
        "        \"Modelo\": nombre,\n",
        "\n",
        "        \"MAE_CV\":\n",
        "            -cv_result[\"test_MAE\"].mean(),\n",
        "\n",
        "        \"MAE_SD\":\n",
        "            cv_result[\"test_MAE\"].std(),\n",
        "\n",
        "        \"RMSE_CV\":\n",
        "            -cv_result[\"test_RMSE\"].mean(),\n",
        "\n",
        "        \"RMSE_SD\":\n",
        "            cv_result[\"test_RMSE\"].std(),\n",
        "\n",
        "        \"R2_CV\":\n",
        "            cv_result[\"test_R2\"].mean(),\n",
        "\n",
        "        \"R2_SD\":\n",
        "            cv_result[\"test_R2\"].std(),\n",
        "\n",
        "        \"Tiempo\":\n",
        "            cv_result[\"fit_time\"].mean()\n",
        "    })"
      ],
      "id": "cee70d43",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Construimos una tabla."
      ],
      "id": "0b17acb4"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "df_resultados = pd.DataFrame(resultados)\n",
        "\n",
        "df_resultados"
      ],
      "id": "78e99d55",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Para facilitar la lectura podemos ordenar por RMSE."
      ],
      "id": "a7a5a0c8"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "df_resultados.sort_values(\"RMSE_CV\")"
      ],
      "id": "a0cc6775",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## ¿Cómo interpretamos la tabla?\n",
        "\n",
        "Tenemos ahora información sobre tres aspectos:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\\boxed{\\text{desempeño promedio}}$$\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\\boxed{\\text{variabilidad entre folds}}$$\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\\boxed{\\text{costo computacional}}.$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Por ejemplo, el RMSE promedio se calcula como\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\\overline{\\operatorname{RMSE}}\n",
        "=\n",
        "\\frac{1}{k}\n",
        "\\sum_{j=1}^{k}\n",
        "\\operatorname{RMSE}_j.$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Mientras que `RMSE_SD` resume cuánto varían esos resultados entre folds.\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.callout-warning icon=\"false\"}\n",
        "## 🧠 Discusión\n",
        "\n",
        "1.  ¿Todos los modelos mejoran la baseline?\n",
        "2.  ¿Los modelos con menor RMSE también presentan mayor $R^2$?\n",
        "3.  ¿Cuál presenta mayor variabilidad entre folds?\n",
        "4.  ¿Existen diferencias importantes en tiempo de entrenamiento?\n",
        "5.  ¿Una diferencia pequeña en RMSE sería suficiente por sí sola para afirmar que dos procedimientos se comportan de manera sustancialmente distinta?\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Visualización de la comparación\n",
        "\n",
        "Representemos el RMSE promedio y su desviación estándar."
      ],
      "id": "def21a1a"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "df_plot = df_resultados.sort_values(\n",
        "    \"RMSE_CV\",\n",
        "    ascending=False\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.figure(figsize=(9, 5))\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.errorbar(\n",
        "    df_plot[\"RMSE_CV\"],\n",
        "    df_plot[\"Modelo\"],\n",
        "    xerr=df_plot[\"RMSE_SD\"],\n",
        "    fmt=\"o\",\n",
        "    capsize=5\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.xlabel(\"RMSE de Cross-Validation\")\n",
        "plt.ylabel(\"Modelo\")\n",
        "plt.title(\"Comparación de modelos\")\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "5d9870a8",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "::: callout-note\n",
        "## Las barras no son intervalos de confianza\n",
        "\n",
        "En esta gráfica las barras representan simplemente la desviación estándar de los resultados obtenidos entre folds.\n",
        "\n",
        "No deben interpretarse automáticamente como intervalos de confianza.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Observar los resultados fold por fold\n",
        "\n",
        "La media puede ocultar información.\n",
        "\n",
        "Comparemos, por ejemplo, Random Forest y Gradient Boosting."
      ],
      "id": "6d039b54"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "modelos_comparar = {\n",
        "    \"Random Forest\": modelos[\"Random Forest\"],\n",
        "    \"Gradient Boosting\": modelos[\"Gradient Boosting\"]\n",
        "}\n",
        "\n",
        "scores_folds = []\n",
        "\n",
        "for nombre, modelo in modelos_comparar.items():\n",
        "\n",
        "    resultado = cross_validate(\n",
        "        modelo,\n",
        "        X_train,\n",
        "        y_train,\n",
        "        cv=cv,\n",
        "        scoring=\"neg_root_mean_squared_error\",\n",
        "        n_jobs=1\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "    for fold, score in enumerate(\n",
        "        -resultado[\"test_score\"],\n",
        "        start=1\n",
        "    ):\n",
        "        scores_folds.append({\n",
        "            \"Modelo\": nombre,\n",
        "            \"Fold\": fold,\n",
        "            \"RMSE\": score\n",
        "        })\n",
        "\n",
        "df_folds = pd.DataFrame(scores_folds)\n",
        "\n",
        "df_folds"
      ],
      "id": "ccc57401",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Visualizamos:"
      ],
      "id": "e470d5fc"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "for nombre in df_folds[\"Modelo\"].unique():\n",
        "\n",
        "    datos = df_folds[\n",
        "        df_folds[\"Modelo\"] == nombre\n",
        "    ]\n",
        "\n",
        "    plt.plot(\n",
        "        datos[\"Fold\"],\n",
        "        datos[\"RMSE\"],\n",
        "        marker=\"o\",\n",
        "        label=nombre\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.xlabel(\"Fold\")\n",
        "plt.ylabel(\"RMSE\")\n",
        "plt.title(\"Desempeño en cada fold\")\n",
        "plt.xticks(range(1, 6))\n",
        "plt.legend()\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "2c4d1082",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "::: {.callout-warning icon=\"false\"}\n",
        "## 🧠 Pregunta\n",
        "\n",
        "¿Uno de los modelos presenta menor RMSE en todos los folds? ¿O las diferencias dependen también de la partición?\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Comparar modelos no termina aquí\n",
        "\n",
        "Hasta ahora hemos utilizado configuraciones razonables, pero no necesariamente optimizadas.\n",
        "\n",
        "Por ejemplo, Gradient Boosting depende de\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\\texttt{learning\\_rate},\n",
        "\\qquad\n",
        "\\texttt{n\\_estimators},\n",
        "\\qquad\n",
        "\\texttt{max\\_depth},\n",
        "\\qquad\n",
        "\\texttt{subsample}.$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Random Forest también posee hiperparámetros como\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\\texttt{n\\_estimators},\n",
        "\\qquad\n",
        "\\texttt{max\\_depth},\n",
        "\\qquad\n",
        "\\texttt{max\\_features},\n",
        "\\qquad\n",
        "\\texttt{min\\_samples\\_leaf}.$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Por ello, una comparación más completa puede incluir un procedimiento de tuning.\n",
        "\n",
        "Para mantener razonable el tiempo de cómputo realizaremos una búsqueda pequeña sobre estos dos modelos.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Tuning de Random Forest\n",
        "\n",
        "Definimos un espacio de búsqueda."
      ],
      "id": "c87705b8"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "param_rf = {\n",
        "    \"n_estimators\": [100, 200, 400],\n",
        "    \"max_depth\": [None, 10, 20, 30],\n",
        "    \"max_features\": [0.5, 0.75, 1.0],\n",
        "    \"min_samples_leaf\": [1, 2, 4]\n",
        "}"
      ],
      "id": "f4d3daa6",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Utilizaremos `RandomizedSearchCV`."
      ],
      "id": "81bed878"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "search_rf = RandomizedSearchCV(\n",
        "    estimator=RandomForestRegressor(\n",
        "        random_state=42,\n",
        "        n_jobs=1\n",
        "    ),\n",
        "    param_distributions=param_rf,\n",
        "    n_iter=12,\n",
        "    scoring=\"neg_root_mean_squared_error\",\n",
        "    cv=cv,\n",
        "    random_state=42,\n",
        "    n_jobs=1\n",
        ")"
      ],
      "id": "fbba2e96",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Ejecutamos:"
      ],
      "id": "51e8b2f7"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "inicio = perf_counter()\n",
        "\n",
        "search_rf.fit(X_train, y_train)\n",
        "\n",
        "tiempo_rf = perf_counter() - inicio"
      ],
      "id": "c3cf7461",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Consultamos los hiperparámetros seleccionados:"
      ],
      "id": "5025a7af"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "search_rf.best_params_"
      ],
      "id": "670bb166",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "y el RMSE:"
      ],
      "id": "86df8e64"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "print(\n",
        "    f\"RMSE CV: {-search_rf.best_score_:.4f}\"\n",
        ")"
      ],
      "id": "ff00af54",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Tuning de Gradient Boosting\n",
        "\n",
        "Definimos ahora:"
      ],
      "id": "02e686c3"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "param_gb = {\n",
        "    \"n_estimators\": [100, 200, 300, 500],\n",
        "    \"learning_rate\": [0.01, 0.03, 0.05, 0.1],\n",
        "    \"max_depth\": [1, 2, 3, 4],\n",
        "    \"subsample\": [0.7, 0.8, 0.9, 1.0]\n",
        "}"
      ],
      "id": "bdb6b7d1",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Construimos la búsqueda."
      ],
      "id": "6cd9c91d"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "search_gb = RandomizedSearchCV(\n",
        "    estimator=GradientBoostingRegressor(\n",
        "        random_state=42\n",
        "    ),\n",
        "    param_distributions=param_gb,\n",
        "    n_iter=12,\n",
        "    scoring=\"neg_root_mean_squared_error\",\n",
        "    cv=cv,\n",
        "    random_state=42,\n",
        "    n_jobs=1\n",
        ")"
      ],
      "id": "81be7dba",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Ejecutamos:"
      ],
      "id": "5b560609"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "inicio = perf_counter()\n",
        "\n",
        "search_gb.fit(X_train, y_train)\n",
        "\n",
        "tiempo_gb = perf_counter() - inicio"
      ],
      "id": "a8394e61",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Consultamos:"
      ],
      "id": "ee02f97a"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "search_gb.best_params_"
      ],
      "id": "5b6e1d9b",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "y:"
      ],
      "id": "8b277d49"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "print(\n",
        "    f\"RMSE CV: {-search_gb.best_score_:.4f}\"\n",
        ")"
      ],
      "id": "bea928a0",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Comparación después del tuning\n",
        "\n",
        "Construimos una tabla pequeña con los dos procedimientos ajustados."
      ],
      "id": "a9487966"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "df_tuning = pd.DataFrame({\n",
        "    \"Modelo\": [\n",
        "        \"Random Forest\",\n",
        "        \"Gradient Boosting\"\n",
        "    ],\n",
        "    \"RMSE_CV\": [\n",
        "        -search_rf.best_score_,\n",
        "        -search_gb.best_score_\n",
        "    ],\n",
        "    \"Tiempo_busqueda\": [\n",
        "        tiempo_rf,\n",
        "        tiempo_gb\n",
        "    ]\n",
        "})\n",
        "\n",
        "df_tuning"
      ],
      "id": "a10c32cf",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Ahora podemos comparar estos resultados con los obtenidos antes del tuning."
      ],
      "id": "2a8fdff8"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "df_resultados[\n",
        "    df_resultados[\"Modelo\"].isin(\n",
        "        [\"Random Forest\", \"Gradient Boosting\"]\n",
        "    )\n",
        "][\n",
        "    [\"Modelo\", \"RMSE_CV\", \"RMSE_SD\"]\n",
        "]"
      ],
      "id": "cb676258",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "::: callout-tip\n",
        "## Tuning no garantiza una mejora enorme\n",
        "\n",
        "La optimización de hiperparámetros puede mejorar el desempeño, pero no debemos esperar necesariamente cambios espectaculares.\n",
        "\n",
        "Si una configuración inicial ya era razonable, la mejora puede ser relativamente pequeña.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## El refit ya ocurrió\n",
        "\n",
        "Recordemos que `RandomizedSearchCV` utiliza por defecto\n",
        "\n",
        "``` text\n",
        "refit=True\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "Después de seleccionar los hiperparámetros, vuelve a entrenar la configuración seleccionada utilizando **todo el conjunto `X_train`**.\n",
        "\n",
        "Por ello tenemos disponibles:"
      ],
      "id": "59f6bad1"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "modelo_rf_final = search_rf.best_estimator_\n",
        "modelo_gb_final = search_gb.best_estimator_"
      ],
      "id": "1f758b64",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Estos modelos ya fueron reajustados con todos los datos de entrenamiento.\n",
        "\n",
        "Hasta este momento:\n",
        "\n",
        "``` text\n",
        "X_test\n",
        "y_test\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "siguen sin participar en ninguna decisión.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Antes de abrir el test\n",
        "\n",
        "Este es un momento importante del flujo de trabajo.\n",
        "\n",
        "Ya realizamos:\n",
        "\n",
        "- comparación inicial;\n",
        "- Cross-Validation;\n",
        "- selección de hiperparámetros;\n",
        "- refit.\n",
        "\n",
        "El conjunto de prueba no participó en ninguna de estas decisiones.\n",
        "\n",
        "Nuestro esquema es:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\\boxed{\n",
        "X_{\\text{train}}\n",
        "}\n",
        "\\longrightarrow\n",
        "\\boxed{\n",
        "\\text{CV + comparación + tuning}\n",
        "}\n",
        "\\longrightarrow\n",
        "\\boxed{\n",
        "\\text{modelo ajustado}\n",
        "}.$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Ahora sí podemos utilizar\n",
        "\n",
        "$$X_{\\text{test}}$$\n",
        "\n",
        "para obtener una evaluación final.\n",
        "\n",
        "::: callout-important\n",
        "## Una vez abierto el test\n",
        "\n",
        "No utilizaremos el resultado de test para volver a modificar repetidamente los hiperparámetros.\n",
        "\n",
        "Si lo hiciéramos, el test comenzaría a funcionar como un nuevo conjunto de validación.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Evaluación final\n",
        "\n",
        "En este ejemplo evaluaremos los dos procedimientos ajustados para observar su comportamiento sobre datos no utilizados durante el desarrollo.\n",
        "\n",
        "Generamos predicciones:"
      ],
      "id": "516c92de"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "pred_rf_test = modelo_rf_final.predict(\n",
        "    X_test\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "pred_gb_test = modelo_gb_final.predict(\n",
        "    X_test\n",
        ")"
      ],
      "id": "e5b523dc",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Crearemos una función para calcular las métricas."
      ],
      "id": "0a982170"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "def metricas_regresion(y_real, y_pred):\n",
        "\n",
        "    mae = mean_absolute_error(\n",
        "        y_real,\n",
        "        y_pred\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "    rmse = np.sqrt(\n",
        "        mean_squared_error(\n",
        "            y_real,\n",
        "            y_pred\n",
        "        )\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "    r2 = r2_score(\n",
        "        y_real,\n",
        "        y_pred\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "    return mae, rmse, r2"
      ],
      "id": "fc37bc1d",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Calculamos:"
      ],
      "id": "b93b4e1c"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "mae_rf, rmse_rf, r2_rf = metricas_regresion(\n",
        "    y_test,\n",
        "    pred_rf_test\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "mae_gb, rmse_gb, r2_gb = metricas_regresion(\n",
        "    y_test,\n",
        "    pred_gb_test\n",
        ")"
      ],
      "id": "fa44b4fe",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Construimos la tabla final."
      ],
      "id": "3ccf71fa"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "resultados_test = pd.DataFrame({\n",
        "    \"Modelo\": [\n",
        "        \"Random Forest\",\n",
        "        \"Gradient Boosting\"\n",
        "    ],\n",
        "\n",
        "    \"MAE_test\": [\n",
        "        mae_rf,\n",
        "        mae_gb\n",
        "    ],\n",
        "\n",
        "    \"RMSE_test\": [\n",
        "        rmse_rf,\n",
        "        rmse_gb\n",
        "    ],\n",
        "\n",
        "    \"R2_test\": [\n",
        "        r2_rf,\n",
        "        r2_gb\n",
        "    ]\n",
        "})\n",
        "\n",
        "resultados_test"
      ],
      "id": "090e922b",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## CV vs. test\n",
        "\n",
        "Comparemos el RMSE estimado durante Cross-Validation con el observado finalmente en test."
      ],
      "id": "fd3e349b"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "comparacion_final = pd.DataFrame({\n",
        "    \"Modelo\": [\n",
        "        \"Random Forest\",\n",
        "        \"Gradient Boosting\"\n",
        "    ],\n",
        "\n",
        "    \"RMSE_CV\": [\n",
        "        -search_rf.best_score_,\n",
        "        -search_gb.best_score_\n",
        "    ],\n",
        "\n",
        "    \"RMSE_test\": [\n",
        "        rmse_rf,\n",
        "        rmse_gb\n",
        "    ]\n",
        "})\n",
        "\n",
        "comparacion_final"
      ],
      "id": "d3a87637",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "No esperamos que\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\\operatorname{RMSE}_{CV}\n",
        "=\n",
        "\\operatorname{RMSE}_{test}$$\n",
        "\n",
        "exactamente.\n",
        "\n",
        "Son estimaciones obtenidas con observaciones y procedimientos diferentes.\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.callout-warning icon=\"false\"}\n",
        "## 🧠 Discusión\n",
        "\n",
        "¿El desempeño en test es razonablemente consistente con lo observado durante Cross-Validation?\n",
        "\n",
        "¿Qué significaría encontrar una diferencia muy grande entre ambos?\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Predicho vs. observado\n",
        "\n",
        "Una métrica resume el desempeño en un único número.\n",
        "\n",
        "Pero también debemos observar las predicciones.\n",
        "\n",
        "Tomemos uno de los modelos finales para ilustrar el diagnóstico. Por ejemplo, Gradient Boosting:"
      ],
      "id": "12220221"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "plt.figure(figsize=(6, 6))\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.scatter(\n",
        "    y_test,\n",
        "    pred_gb_test,\n",
        "    alpha=0.3\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "limites = [\n",
        "    min(y_test.min(), pred_gb_test.min()),\n",
        "    max(y_test.max(), pred_gb_test.max())\n",
        "]\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.plot(\n",
        "    limites,\n",
        "    limites,\n",
        "    linestyle=\"--\"\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.xlabel(\"Valor observado\")\n",
        "plt.ylabel(\"Valor predicho\")\n",
        "plt.title(\"Observado vs. predicho\")\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "f9954f38",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "La línea punteada representa\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\\widehat y=y.$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Predicciones perfectas caerían exactamente sobre esta línea.\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.callout-warning icon=\"false\"}\n",
        "## 🧠 Observa\n",
        "\n",
        "¿Las predicciones se distribuyen aproximadamente alrededor de la diagonal?\n",
        "\n",
        "¿En qué regiones parecen existir mayores errores?\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Residuos\n",
        "\n",
        "Definimos los residuos como\n",
        "\n",
        "$$e_i\n",
        "=\n",
        "y_i-\\widehat y_i.$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Calculamos:"
      ],
      "id": "427b2cdf"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "residuos = y_test - pred_gb_test"
      ],
      "id": "4dcadab5",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Veamos su distribución."
      ],
      "id": "51fc561b"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "plt.figure(figsize=(7, 4))\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.hist(\n",
        "    residuos,\n",
        "    bins=30\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.xlabel(\"Residuo\")\n",
        "plt.ylabel(\"Frecuencia\")\n",
        "plt.title(\"Distribución de los residuos\")\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "9cc18009",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "También podemos representar residuos contra predicciones."
      ],
      "id": "da0eb63a"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "plt.figure(figsize=(7, 5))\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.scatter(\n",
        "    pred_gb_test,\n",
        "    residuos,\n",
        "    alpha=0.3\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.axhline(\n",
        "    0,\n",
        "    linestyle=\"--\"\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.xlabel(\"Valor predicho\")\n",
        "plt.ylabel(\"Residuo\")\n",
        "plt.title(\"Residuos vs. valores predichos\")\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "54d27109",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Una gráfica de residuos puede revelar patrones que una métrica agregada no muestra.\n",
        "\n",
        "::: callout-note\n",
        "## Las métricas no sustituyen el diagnóstico\n",
        "\n",
        "Dos modelos pueden tener valores similares de RMSE y, sin embargo, cometer errores de maneras diferentes.\n",
        "\n",
        "Por eso conviene complementar las métricas con visualizaciones y análisis del error.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## ¿Dónde se equivoca más el modelo?\n",
        "\n",
        "Podemos construir una tabla con las predicciones y sus errores."
      ],
      "id": "8626a737"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "diagnostico = X_test.copy()\n",
        "\n",
        "diagnostico[\"y_real\"] = y_test\n",
        "diagnostico[\"y_pred\"] = pred_gb_test\n",
        "diagnostico[\"residuo\"] = (\n",
        "    diagnostico[\"y_real\"]\n",
        "    - diagnostico[\"y_pred\"]\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "diagnostico[\"error_absoluto\"] = (\n",
        "    diagnostico[\"residuo\"].abs()\n",
        ")"
      ],
      "id": "f9615293",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Observemos las predicciones con mayor error absoluto."
      ],
      "id": "9bc0371d"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "diagnostico.sort_values(\n",
        "    \"error_absoluto\",\n",
        "    ascending=False\n",
        ").head(10)"
      ],
      "id": "15236d85",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Esto permite pasar de la pregunta\n",
        "\n",
        "> ¿Cuál es el RMSE?\n",
        "\n",
        "a otra pregunta potencialmente más interesante:\n",
        "\n",
        "> ¿En qué observaciones se está equivocando el modelo?\n",
        "\n",
        "## Error y localización geográfica\n",
        "\n",
        "Como California Housing contiene coordenadas geográficas, podemos explorar espacialmente el error."
      ],
      "id": "5680be34"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "plt.figure(figsize=(8, 6))\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.scatter(\n",
        "    diagnostico[\"Longitude\"],\n",
        "    diagnostico[\"Latitude\"],\n",
        "    c=diagnostico[\"error_absoluto\"],\n",
        "    s=10,\n",
        "    alpha=0.6\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.xlabel(\"Longitude\")\n",
        "plt.ylabel(\"Latitude\")\n",
        "plt.title(\"Distribución geográfica del error absoluto\")\n",
        "plt.colorbar(label=\"Error absoluto\")\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "5d6b344c",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "::: {.callout-warning icon=\"false\"}\n",
        "## 🧠 Pregunta\n",
        "\n",
        "¿Los errores parecen distribuirse uniformemente? ¿Observas regiones donde el modelo parece tener mayores dificultades?\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "Este tipo de análisis puede revelar estructura que una única métrica no muestra.\n",
        "\n",
        "## El flujo completo\n",
        "\n",
        "Ya podemos representar todo el procedimiento realizado durante las tres prácticas.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Paso 1: separar los datos\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\\mathcal{D}\n",
        "\\longrightarrow\n",
        "\\boxed{\n",
        "\\mathcal{D}_{\\text{train}}\n",
        "}\n",
        "+\n",
        "\\boxed{\n",
        "\\mathcal{D}_{\\text{test}}\n",
        "}.$$\n",
        "\n",
        "### Paso 2: trabajar solamente con train\n",
        "\n",
        "Dentro de $\\mathcal{D}_{\\text{train}}$ realizamos:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\\text{Cross-Validation}\n",
        "\\longrightarrow\n",
        "\\text{comparación}\n",
        "\\longrightarrow\n",
        "\\text{tuning}.$$\n",
        "\n",
        "### Paso 3: seleccionar hiperparámetros\n",
        "\n",
        "Por ejemplo:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\\boldsymbol{\\lambda}^{*}\n",
        "=\n",
        "\\arg\\min_{\\boldsymbol{\\lambda}}\n",
        "\\operatorname{RMSE}_{CV}(\\boldsymbol{\\lambda}).$$\n",
        "\n",
        "### Paso 4: refit\n",
        "\n",
        "El procedimiento seleccionado se vuelve a entrenar utilizando todo\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\\mathcal{D}_{\\text{train}}.$$\n",
        "\n",
        "### Paso 5: evaluación final\n",
        "\n",
        "Finalmente:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\\widehat f^{*}(X_{\\text{test}})$$\n",
        "\n",
        "permite calcular\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\\operatorname{MAE}_{test},\n",
        "\\qquad\n",
        "\\operatorname{RMSE}_{test},\n",
        "\\qquad\n",
        "R^2_{\\text{test}}.$$\n",
        "\n",
        "::: callout-tip\n",
        "## La idea central de la unidad\n",
        "\n",
        "El objetivo no es encontrar el modelo que produzca el número más pequeño en una tabla.\n",
        "\n",
        "El objetivo es construir un procedimiento de evaluación en el que cada conjunto de datos tenga una función clara y donde las decisiones de modelado no contaminen la evaluación final.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Ejercicio integrador\n",
        "\n",
        "Ahora realizarás el mismo flujo utilizando **XGBoost**.\n",
        "\n",
        "Importa:\n",
        "\n",
        "``` python\n",
        "from xgboost import XGBRegressor\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "Define inicialmente:\n",
        "\n",
        "``` python\n",
        "xgb = XGBRegressor(\n",
        "    objective=\"reg:squarederror\",\n",
        "    random_state=42,\n",
        "    n_jobs=1\n",
        ")\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "Utiliza el siguiente espacio:\n",
        "\n",
        "``` python\n",
        "param_xgb = {\n",
        "    \"n_estimators\": [100, 200, 300, 500],\n",
